      "native_2025_2026_technosphere_vectors_equal": true,
      "limitations": "Use the complete native RER tap-water inventory per signed kg delivered to the consumer, factor +1, replacing the earlier CH supplier for this Europe-without-Switzerland market. Native RER is itself a CH/DE-based approximation extrapolated to Europe, not an exact country or regional resource model. It includes treatment chemicals, electricity, water works, pumping/storage/network infrastructure, transport, wastewater and direct water flows; preserve the whole native model once. The inspected source has eight direct water producers summing to 1 kg and a separate 0.12867 kg recursive input from the same market. The sum 1.12867 kg is not a direct producer-only loss coefficient. Do not multiply the delivered-kg demand by a source water-production, recursive-supply or distribution-loss factor, and do not append the source loop or add another native network/withdrawal/treatment step. Source recursion and native own water balance differ, with unquantified score effects. Preserve caller signs, supported uncertainty, formulas and ownership. The reference is kg of delivered potable water, not cubic metres of abstraction or a treatment-only service. No density conversion or water-balance correction is introduced; separately listed caller water, transport and emissions remain separate. Source treatment shares, pressure assumptions, resource/return geography, losses, network, electricity, allocation, vintage and uncertainty differ. Native RER uses 0.00039 kWh of European electricity per kg; the earlier CH supplier uses 0.00042889 kWh of Swiss electricity. Regionalized water-stress or LCIA equivalence is not established; native biosphere exclusions and unquantified score effects remain warnings. The requested 3.7 permission is retained using the inspected 3.7.1 functional-reference witness and matching adjacent definitions. Unpatched 3.7 coefficients were not inspected, source contexts are not relabeled, and no coefficient or impact equality is claimed. Exact 3.7.1/other patch callers, inverse correspondences and cross-system-model conversions are not implicitly approved.",
